  "description": "<p>Curl the headers on any /fcr:versions uri and you'll notice that there are no link headers as I would expect.</p>\n\n<p>Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Resource\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Resource</a>&gt;;rel=\"type\"<br/>\nLink: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#RDFSource\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#RDFSource</a>&gt;;rel=\"type\"</p>\n\n<p>To reproduce:</p>\n\n<p>1. Create a resource and then add a version to that resource.<br/>\n2. curl -v     -X HEAD -i <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/your-resource/fcr:versions\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/your-resource/fcr:versions</a><br/>\n3. verify there are no links returned.</p>",
